# Known-answer tests for the standalone hash modules

Every theorem is `native_decide`: the copied hash code computing the
FIPS-correct digest on a fixed input IS the proof — no sorry, no
hypotheses. Digest literals were generated in Python (hashlib /
pycryptodome) from the exact inputs named; the SHA-256 V1-01 shape theorem
re-derives ERC-8441 V1-01's `base` line, and the SHA3-256 theorem checks
the V3-05 combiner-input shape.
-/

